
+ Development approach ...

  + Edit, build, view locally
  + Commit edits that work
  + Push to github (auto publish in github pages)
  + Release on github major milestones (e.g., version 1)


+ NOTE that with modern browsers need to run a local server to 
  view local files (to avoid CORS errors)

  npx http-server _book -o -p 9999 

  Ctrl-C to shut down, or if running in bg use this to find process id

  lsof -i :9999


+ Note this possible approach for adding "Reference" and "Footnote" titles
  to sections at the end of each chapter

  https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli/discussions/11765#discussioncomment-11711801


+ Attempt at describing a framework for designing and evaluating
  data visualisations

  Needs a better name ...


+ Also first attempt at using Quarto

  install.packages("quarto")
  quarto::quarto_render("hello.qmd")


+ Possible "publication" route ...

  Use Quarto or Bookdown to create a website + host it on GitHub Pages
  https://quarto.org/docs/publishing/github-pages.html

  Upload a copy of the PDF to Zenodo to get a DOI
  Link the Zenodo DOI in your website's sidebar. 
  OR can link my Uni Figshare to github (=> DOI) and then auto-publish
  via github releases
  https://info.figshare.com/user-guide/how-to-connect-figshare-with-your-github-account/


